{"id": "EUVD-2026-97371", "enisaUuid": "59c1273f-f56d-3f46-b3da-e807949d6384", "description": "TDuck survey form through 6.0 contains a broken access control vulnerability that allows authenticated users to add fields to other users' forms via POST /user/form/item/batch/create. Attackers can submit an array whose first element references their own form and later elements reference a victim's formKey, injecting attacker-chosen fields onto the victim's public fill page.", "datePublished": "2026-10-12T13:10:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T17:41:17", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:N/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/AnkesKasty/cve-request-poc/blob/a7b6d1423555812d8efa26c91c5d0683164b31e5/tduck/poc_form_item_batch_create_cross_form.py", "https://github.com/TDuckCloud/tduck-survey-form/blob/43ffa9c993e38936fc4de7d8e5aee82bbaa19502/tduck-api/src/main/java/com/tduck/cloud/api/web/controller/UserFormController.java#L327-L336", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/tduck-survey-form-through-6.0-authorization-bypass-via-user-controlled-form-key-in-post-user-form-item-batch-create"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-109165", "GHSA-xjj9-v7hq-9hc8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "f6769b12-2ca6-3f44-bf0c-4138f684779c", "product": {"name": "tduck-survey-form", "vendor": {"name": "TDuckCloud"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22646.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "746af676-dfb7-3f35-a207-7ca989f12a99", "vendor": {"name": "TDuckCloud"}}], "isExploited": false}